  "body": "Part of #894.\n\nAfter #894's first slice a thread mill is simulated and drawn as plain cylinders:\n- the program simulation sweeps its tooth roots (`operation::tool_law::cutting_radius`, the tap's reading from #266), so the simulated stock shows a threaded hole at its minor diameter and no thread;\n- `Tool::profile` (the editor preview, the simulation's tool body) draws the cylinder the tooth crests sweep - no teeth, and no neck unless a cutter outline is drawn by hand (#93).\n\nThe gouge laws do judge the form at two levels (crests against the major circle, roots against the part - `operation::thread_op`), so this is a display and rest-material gap, not an unchecked cut.\n\n**What is missing**\n- A sweep atom for the toothed profile on a helical arc (the V rows revolved and swept), in the field and column engines, so the stock shows the thread and a helix that is off pitch shows as damaged flanks.\n- A toothed side view for the two thread-mill kinds in `Tool::profile` / the spun cutter outline (rows at the pitch on a multi-form mill, one tooth on a single-form mill), agreeing with the bands the reach laws read.\n\n**Done means:** simulating a thread-milling program shows the helical thread in the stock; a path whose lead differs from the tool's pitch on a multi-form mill shows cut flanks in the deviation view; the tool preview draws the teeth; pinned by tests.\n",
